\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Do unit-demand capacity instances on unbounded vertex counts n have Goemans–Linial semidefinite integrality gap at least $c\surd \log (n)/(\log $ $\log (n))^{3}$ for one absolute $c>0$, with positive relaxation value?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Do unit-demand capacity instances on unbounded vertex counts n have Goemans–Linial semidefinite integrality gap at least $c\surd \log (n)/(\log $ $\log (n))^{3}$ for one absolute $c>0$, with positive relaxation value?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://afonsobandeira.wordpress.com/2015/10/05/10l42pcheeger/}.
